WEBVTT

NOTE Scene 04B. Speaker labels and dialogue derive from the original script.
NOTE Time positions aligned using faster-whisper word timestamps; human review still required.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
<v Jack Marlowe>Vivian telephoned Sterling and offered to sell him the hat.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:08.940
<v Jack Marlowe>He chose a warehouse by the river. Betty confirmed the original ledger was in

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.620
<v Jack Marlowe>the attorney's hands and arrived with our decoy.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:15.540
<v Betty>Seventy-five cents, boss. I got it half price.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.380
<v Jack Marlowe>What's wrong with it?

00:00:17.732 --> 00:00:19.920
<v Betty>Nothin', if ya don't mind the smell.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.400
<v Vivian Cross>Darling, this is positively revolting.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.180
<v Betty>For seventy-five cents, it can be anythin' it wants.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.080
<v Jack Marlowe>Vivian, give Sterling the hat only after he explains what he wanted from Ernest.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.380
<v Jack Marlowe>Betty and I will be behind those crates. The attorney's waiting for our call.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.060
<v Vivian Cross>Don't worry, detective. I've been getting men to tell me things they shouldn't

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:41.700
<v Vivian Cross>for years.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.340
<v Betty>Yeah, I bet.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.720
<v Jack Marlowe>We took our positions. A few minutes later, Sterling arrived with Knuckles, whose

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.660
<v Jack Marlowe>footsteps sounded like a piano being delivered upstairs.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.080
<v Victor Sterling>Mrs. Cross. Where is the evidence?

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.960
<v Vivian Cross>Inside the hat, darling. Just as you requested.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:00.620
<v Victor Sterling>Let me see it.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:05.620
<v Vivian Cross>First, tell me what my husband discovered. A girl likes to know what she's selling.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.680
<v Victor Sterling>Your husband lacked imagination. The insurance companies were simply a convenient

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.560
<v Victor Sterling>means of transferring money to my personal accounts.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.840
<v Vivian Cross>And when Ernest found out?

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:21.460
<v Victor Sterling>He threatened to expose me. I had Knuckles search his apartment for the evidence.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.400
<v Victor Sterling>Apparently that was beyond his capabilities.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.520
<v Knuckles Malone>Hey, I found the hat, didn't I? Eventually.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:28.680
<v Knuckles Malone>Sorta.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:33.080
<v Vivian Cross>So if you destroy the paper inside this hat, nobody can find the ledger?

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:37.140
<v Victor Sterling>Precisely. And now, our transaction is concluded.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.080
<v Vivian Cross>Here you are, darling.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:43.560
<v Victor Sterling>Eggs. Milk. Two pounds of potatoes. What is this?

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:46.780
<v Betty>Aw, nuts! I wondered where that went.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:48.040
<v Victor Sterling>Who's there?!

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:53.620
<v Jack Marlowe>Good evening, Sterling. We have the ledger. And now two witnesses to your confession.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.920
<v Victor Sterling>Knuckles! Do something!

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.960
<v Knuckles Malone>Look, detective, I'm willin' to testify.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:00.460
<v Victor Sterling>You traitor!

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:05.220
<v Knuckles Malone>Hey! I been workin' overtime for six months and ya still owe me twelve bucks!

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.260
<v Vivian Cross>Victor, darling. You really ought to treat your employees better.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:11.880
<v Betty>And pay 'em! You hear that, boss?

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:15.220
<v Jack Marlowe>I'm beginning to regret bringing you along.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.040
<v Victor Sterling>Very well. I'll speak to my attorney.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.520
<v Jack Marlowe>Sterling agreed to cooperate with the authorities.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:26.660
<v Jack Marlowe>The district attorney had the evidence, Betty had her grocery list, and Knuckles

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:29.260
<v Jack Marlowe>had discovered the joys of collective bargaining.

